/-- MathArena Problem (id=MathArena_smt_2025_51, dataset=MathArena_smt_2025, idx=51 )
    Informal statement: Define a sequence $\left\{a_{n}\right\}$ by $a_{1}=5$ and $a_{n+1}=\frac{5 a_{n}+\sqrt{21 a_{n}^{2}+4}}{2}$ for $n \geq 1$. Compute the value of

$$
\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{1}{a_{n} a_{n+1}}
$$
    Answer: \frac{23-5 \sqrt{21}}{10}
-/
